%description:

DcTcp.g:invalid -- a gain of 0 stops the run with an error.

The claim: the code accepts a gain above 0 and at most 1.

The classes: rfc8257 (1/16, the default of RFC 8257 section 4.2), other (another value up to
1), invalid (0 and less, above 1). The code: DcTcp updates alpha once each window,
alpha = alpha * (1 - g) + g * F, from 0, and emits it as calcLoad (DcTcp::processEce()).

Host under test: host1, with DcTcp. Observation: the error, and the exit code of the run.

%# parameter: DcTcp.g
%# class: invalid
%# value: 0
%# key: *.host1.tcp.conn-*.algorithm.g
%# expected-result: PASS

%activity:
EV << "DcTcpGInvalid compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.conn-*.algorithm.g = 0    # the parameter under test
*.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass = "DcTcp"
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%exitcode: 1

%contains-regex: stderr
g must be more than 0 and at most 1, but it is 0
